public class OpportunityPipelineHandler {
    private static Boolean isRunning = false;

    public static void handle(List<Opportunity> newOpps, List<Opportunity> oldOpps) {
        if (isRunning) {
            return;
        }
        isRunning = true;
        try {
            Boolean isDelete = (newOpps == null);
            Boolean isUpdate = (newOpps != null && oldOpps != null);

            Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();

            if (!isDelete) {
                for (Opportunity o : newOpps) {
                    if (o.AccountId != null) {
                        accountIds.add(o.AccountId);
                    }
                }
            }

            if (isUpdate) {
                for (Integer i = 0; i < oldOpps.size(); i++) {
                    if (oldOpps[i].AccountId != null && oldOpps[i].AccountId != newOpps[i].AccountId) {
                        accountIds.add(oldOpps[i].AccountId);
                    }
                }
            }

            if (isDelete) {
                for (Opportunity o : oldOpps) {
                    if (o.AccountId != null) {
                        accountIds.add(o.AccountId);
                    }
                }
            }

            if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
                return;
            }

            Map<Id, Account> accountMap = new Map<Id, Account>(
                [SELECT Id, FB_Open_Pipeline__c, FB_Open_Opportunities__c
                 FROM Account
                 WHERE Id IN :accountIds]
            );

            List<Opportunity> openOpps = [
                SELECT AccountId, Amount
                FROM Opportunity
                WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds AND IsClosed = false
            ];

            Map<Id, Decimal> pipelineTotals = new Map<Id, Decimal>();
            Map<Id, Integer> oppCounts = new Map<Id, Integer>();
            for (Opportunity o : openOpps) {
                Decimal amt = (o.Amount == null) ? 0 : o.Amount;
                Decimal curTotal = pipelineTotals.get(o.AccountId);
                pipelineTotals.put(o.AccountId, (curTotal == null ? 0 : curTotal) + amt);
                Integer curCount = oppCounts.get(o.AccountId);
                oppCounts.put(o.AccountId, (curCount == null ? 0 : curCount) + 1);
            }

            List<Account> toUpdate = new List<Account>();
            for (Id accId : accountIds) {
                Account acc = accountMap.get(accId);
                if (acc == null) {
                    continue;
                }
                Decimal newPipeline = pipelineTotals.get(accId);
                if (newPipeline == null) {
                    newPipeline = 0;
                }
                Integer newCount = oppCounts.get(accId);
                if (newCount == null) {
                    newCount = 0;
                }

                if (acc.FB_Open_Pipeline__c != newPipeline || acc.FB_Open_Opportunities__c != newCount) {
                    acc.FB_Open_Pipeline__c = newPipeline;
                    acc.FB_Open_Opportunities__c = newCount;
                    toUpdate.add(acc);
                }
            }

            if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
                update toUpdate;
            }
        } finally {
            isRunning = false;
        }
    }
}
```

**What changed and why:**

- **`Trigger.*` is not accessible outside a trigger file.** The fix passes `Trigger.new` and `Trigger.old` as parameters to the handler. Inside the handler, the operation context is inferred from null-ness: `newOpps == null` → delete; both non-null → update; `oldOpps == null` → insert/undelete.

- **Re-entrancy guard:** When `update toUpdate` fires `AccountTrigger` → `update opps` → `OpportunityTrigger` → `handle()`, the `isRunning` flag (still true inside the `try`) causes the nested call to return immediately. The `finally` block resets it so subsequent top-level DML statements in the same transaction are handled correctly.

- **Bulk-safe:** At most 2 SOQL queries and 1 DML per trigger invocation, all bounded by the affected-account set (≤ 200 + a few for moves).

- **Correctness after every DML:** Each trigger firing re-queries open opportunities for the affected accounts and computes totals from scratch—no delta bookkeeping that could drift across multiple DML statements.

- **Zero-not-null:** When no open opportunities exist for an account, `pipelineTotals`/`oppCounts` have no entry → defaults to `0`. The comparison `null != 0` is `true` in Apex, forcing the update so the fields show `0` rather than remaining blank.

