## What I'd change and why

**The SOQL-in-a-loop in `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(Id)`.**

Each call executes a separate `SELECT … FROM Product2 WHERE Id = :productId`. With 200 line items in a single CPQ insert, the handler fires 200 SOQL statements → **Limit Exceeded: SOQL queries** (100/tx). The same problem would hit any `before update` / `before undelete` context if the trigger is extended.

**Recommended fix (one new method added to `PricingRules`, existing method untouched):**

```apex
/** Bulk: standard discount (percent) for a set of product Ids – one query. */
public static Map<Id, Decimal> standardDiscountFor(Set<Id> productIds) {
    Map<Id, Decimal> result = new Map<Id, Decimal>();
    if (productIds == null || productIds.isEmpty()) return result;

    List<Product2> products = [SELECT Id, Family FROM Product2 WHERE Id IN :productIds];
    for (Product2 p : products) {
        result.put(p.Id, standardDiscountForFamily(p.Family));
    }
    return result;
}
```

The handler then batches the lookup:

```apex
