```apex
public class CaseSurveyDispatcher implements Queueable {
    private final List<Id> caseIds;

    public CaseSurveyDispatcher(List<Id> caseIds) {
        this.caseIds = caseIds;
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        if (caseIds == null || caseIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Governor limit: max 50 System.enqueueJob calls per transaction.
        // When we still have work to chain, reserve one slot for the
        // next dispatcher: 49 jobs + 1 dispatcher = 50 calls.
        // On the final batch we can use all 50 slots for jobs.
        Integer batchSize = (caseIds.size() > 50) ? 49 : caseIds.size();

        for (Integer i = 0; i < batchSize; i++) {
            System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(caseIds[i]));
        }

        if (caseIds.size() > batchSize) {
            System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyDispatcher(
                caseIds.sublist(batchSize, caseIds.size())
            ));
        }
    }
}
```

## What changed and why

| Change | Reason |
|--------|--------|
| Trigger now enqueues **one** `CaseSurveyDispatcher` instead of N individual jobs | Calling `System.enqueueJob` 200 times in a single trigger transaction throws `LimitException` (max 50). A single dispatcher call stays well within the limit regardless of how many cases are closed. |
| New `CaseSurveyDispatcher` Queueable | Iterates the Id list in chunks of ≤ 50, enqueuing a `CaseSurveyJob` per case. If Ids remain, it enqueues a *second* dispatcher with the tail. Each chunk is its own transaction, so the 50-call ceiling is never exceeded. |
| `CaseSurveyJob` re-queries the Case at execution time | The job runs asynchronously; the record could be deleted or its `ContactId` cleared before the job fires. The null-guards prevent a `QueryException` or a Task with a null `WhoId`. |
| Each case still gets its **own** `CaseSurveyJob` | A `DmlException` on one Task (validation rule, duplicate, etc.) fails only that job's transaction and does not affect the others—exactly the isolation the requirement calls for. |

### Worked example (200 cases)

| Dispatcher # | Jobs enqueued | Chained? | Total calls |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 49 | yes (151 remaining) | 50 |
| 2 | 49 | yes (102 remaining) | 50 |
| 3 | 49 | yes (53 remaining) | 50 |
| 4 | 49 | yes (4 remaining) | 50 |
| 5 | 4 | no | 4 |

Total `CaseSurveyJob` instances: 49 × 4 + 4 = **200** ✓ — no `LimitException`.

